Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] ANOVA loop
Message-ID: <ZDXFoZOb0yw.qL4hgJOFh8gJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/ZDXFoZOb0yw/m/qL4hgJOFh8gJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Say y is a phenotype of length n and X is a matrix of genotypes of dimension n x p.

  pval <- apply(X, 2, function(gen,phe)
                  anova(aov(phe ~ gen))[1,5], y)

You may need to use as.factor(gen), as follows:

  pval <- apply(X, 2, function(gen,phe)
                  anova(aov(phe ~ as.factor(gen)))[1,5], y)

As a for loop:

  pval <- rep(NA, ncol(X))
  for(i in 1:ncol(gen))
    pval[i] <- anova(aov(y ~ as.factor(X[,i])))[1,5]

karl

